        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Time the jerk before you fix it.</strong> Once per belt
            revolution is the belt or a roller; with each footstrike is friction or tension; a speed
            that changes on its own is the sensor, brushes, wiring or controller.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Surging means stop</strong> — unplug it and call support. For a
            footstrike stutter, start with the deck, not the bolts, using our guide to a
            <a href="/treadmill-belt-slows-down-when-i-step-on-it/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">belt that slows when you step on it</a>.
          </p>
